{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaReebSinhParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaReebSinhParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Inverse","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qbeta_phase_leading_sq_eq_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qbeta_phase_leading_sq_eq_two","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaReebSinhParity.lean#L116-L122","doc":"**`Φ₁² = 2` from `c_2 = −1`.** With the u² coefficient `c_2 = −Φ₁²/2`\nset to the Lean-proved value `−1`, the leading phase coefficient satisfies\n`Φ₁² = 2` — i.e. `Φ₁ = √2` (the fibre `cos(√2·u)` slice; the imaginary\nhyperbolic angle `i√2` of the bar-even `cosh` channel). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qbeta_phase_cos_truncation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qbeta_phase_cos_truncation","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaReebSinhParity.lean#L102-L114","doc":"**Phase ↔ (c_2, c_3) algebraic core.** For the truncated cosine phase\n`P(u) = 1 − (Φ₁u + Φ₂u²)²/2`, the order-u² coefficient is `−Φ₁²/2` and the\norder-u³ coefficient is `−Φ₁·Φ₂` (the rest is the `−Φ₂²/2·u⁴` tail):\n\n  `1 − (Φ₁u + Φ₂u²)²/2 = 1 − (Φ₁²/2)·u² − (Φ₁·Φ₂)·u³ − (Φ₂²/2)·u⁴`.\n\nReading coefficients: `c_2 = −Φ₁²/2` (⇒ `Φ₁² = 2` from the proved\n`c_2 = −1`) and `c_3 = −Φ₁·Φ₂` (the odd-rung reduction `c_3 = g` of\nPR #1880, with `g = −Φ₁·Φ₂`). One-line `ring` identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.reeb_cosh_only_no_bar_antisymmetric_part","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.reeb_cosh_only_no_bar_antisymmetric_part","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaReebSinhParity.lean#L80-L88","doc":"**Corollary: a bar-symmetric (cosh-only) Reeb scalar has zero\nbar-antisymmetric part.** Setting `b = 0` in the split above: a pure\n`cosh` Reeb holonomy contributes nothing to c_3 — the formal statement of\n\"the cosh/even component cannot source the first bar-antisymmetric\ncoefficient.\" ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.reeb_holonomy_bar_antisymmetric_part","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.reeb_holonomy_bar_antisymmetric_part","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaReebSinhParity.lean#L61-L78","doc":"**Reeb-holonomy parity split.** Write a Reeb holonomy scalar as\n`H(η) = a · cosh(k·η) + b · sinh(k·η)` (the `cosh`/`sinh` decomposition of\nthe hyperbolic flow). Its bar-conjugate `H(-η)` keeps the `cosh` term and\nflips the `sinh` term:\n\n  `H(-η) = a · cosh(k·η) − b · sinh(k·η)`.\n\nHence the **bar-antisymmetric part** `(H(η) − H(-η))/2 = b · sinh(k·η)` is\ncarried entirely by the `sinh` component. A bar-antisymmetric coefficient\n(c_3) can only come from `b · sinh(k·η)` — the cosh part is parity-blocked,\nexactly as the even cos/cosh avatars were (PR #1866). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.reeb_sinh_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.reeb_sinh_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaReebSinhParity.lean#L54-L59","doc":"**Reeb sinh component is bar-odd.** `sinh(k·η)` flips sign under the bar\ninvolution `η ↦ -η`, making it the only parity-admissible source for a\nbar-antisymmetric coefficient such as c_3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.reeb_cosh_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.reeb_cosh_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaReebSinhParity.lean#L47-L52","doc":"**Reeb cosh component is bar-even.** `cosh(k·η)` is invariant under the\nbar involution `η ↦ -η`, hence sources only bar-symmetric coefficients\n(the c_2 = -1 rung). ","signatureChunk":0}]}